 "notes": [
  "No davwheat seed existed for CZ; compiled from scratch.",
  "ČTÚ's review conclusions of 13 Aug 2026 give exact block edges and validity for 800, 1800 and 2600 MHz. It proposes new 20-year assignments for the same blocks from 1 Jul 2029 to 30 Jun 2049; this is a draft for consultation and is not drawn as a future entry.",
  "900 MHz edges come from ČTÚ's 2024 review. O2 and T-Mobile renewed 900/1800 in 2024 until 31 Dec 2044; Vodafone renewed in 2025 until 30 Jun 2049. The 2026 ČTÚ document confirms the 1800 split.",
  "3.4–3.8 GHz: ČTÚ fixed the layout on 11 Aug 2021 (Incrate 3400–3480, T-Mobile 3480–3540, Vodafone 3540–3600, PODA 3600–3640, O2 3640–3700, Nordic Telecom 5G 3700–3800). Two transfers followed: Incrate's block went to T-Mobile (Lupa.cz, Jul 2023), and Nordic's block went to O2 in 2024 before PPF/O2 bought Nordic Telecom in 2025 (Lupa.cz).",
  "2100 MHz: three 2×20 MHz blocks renewed until 31 Dec 2041 (O2 in Dec 2021, Vodafone from 24 Feb 2025). The operator order comes from gsmweb.cz only.",
  "spectrum-tracker lists Vodafone 900 as 880.1–890 MHz (2×9.9). ČTÚ says 880.1–890.1 MHz (2×10); ČTÚ is used.",
  "Expiry dates for 700 MHz and 3.4–3.8 GHz were not found and are left out.",
  "Corrected after independent verification (2026-09-28): 3600–3640 MHz belongs to Vodafone (bought from PODA in early 2023; Lupa.cz, gsmweb.cz), giving Vodafone 100 MHz at 3.5 GHz."
 ],
 "missing": [
  "700 MHz and 3.4–3.8 GHz licence expiry dates",
  "2100 MHz block-to-operator mapping confirmed by only one non-regulator source (gsmweb.cz)",
  "Status of PODA's 3600–3640 MHz in 2026 not re-confirmed after 2021",
  "Carrier EARFCN/NR-ARFCN not compiled"
 ],
